-- title:
--   Initial ordered partition complexes generated by a pattern
-- statement:
--   For an ordered hypergraph pattern over a finite vertex type, each top-face edge predicate has a finite support. The partition generated by that support distinguishes membership in the edge set from nonmembership, with empty cells discarded by the finite-partition construction.
--
--   The bundle also defines the complex that is indiscrete at every face and rank. The canonical initial complex replaces its top layer by the pattern-generated partitions while leaving all lower layers indiscrete. This retains exactly the input edge information needed to start the regularity construction.
